{
 "film": "molasses",
 "source": [
  "On January 15, 1919, a steel tank burst on the Boston waterfront.",
  "It stood 50 feet tall and held 2.3 million gallons of molasses.",
  "At about 12:30 in the afternoon it collapsed, and a wave 25 feet high ran through the North End.",
  "The wave moved at an estimated 35 miles an hour.",
  "It drove steel panels of the tank against the girders of the elevated railway.",
  "21 people died, and about 150 were injured.",
  "First to the scene were 116 cadets from a training ship docked nearby.",
  "The next day, the Boston Post ran it across the front page.",
  "119 residents sued the company that owned the tank.",
  "After three years of hearings, it was found responsible and paid $628,000 in damages."
 ],
